Changes in version 0.99.71 (2026-11-25)
+ plotTransitionMatrix draws the transitions as a graph of states
  (layout = "graph")
+ plotTimeEffect draws its line at null.value, such as 1 for a ratio

Changes in version 0.99.70 (2026-11-25)
+ plotLagProfile draws the variogram fitted by miaTime::getVariogramModel()
  (model, period)

Changes in version 0.99.69 (2026-11-23)
+ Reference index of the pkgdown site grouped by question, Bootstrap 5
+ BiocCheck notes addressed: R >= 4.6.0, no suppressWarnings() in
  plotTrend, shorter helpers for events and plotOrigin

Changes in version 0.99.68 (2026-11-23)
+ New plots: plotProfiles (feature trajectory clusters), plotTimeline (one
  subject as stacked tracks), plotRuns (durations of presence or states),
  plotStates (state shares per subject), plotRmcorr (repeated-measures
  correlation), plotChanges (distribution of abundance changes),
  plotPartner and plotOrigin (mother-infant, donor-recipient designs) and
  plotNoise (noise colour of each subject's features)
+ plotNetwork draws a matrix of interaction strengths (layout = "matrix")
+ plotTiles draws categorical results, such as strains
+ plotIndividuality draws within- and between-subject dissimilarity over
  time windows (layout = "time")
+ plotTimeEffect draws permutation curves (null), p-values (p.col) and
  points sized by a column (size.by)
+ plotTrend splits a feature into prevalence and values above detection
  (detection); with align.to, fits stop at the event; events of single
  subjects are drawn in their panels
+ plotLagProfile draws autocorrelation tables; plotSpectrum tapers each
  series before the periodogram, which changes its spectra slightly, and
  fits the log-log slope (fit = "power")
+ plotTrend: a column starting with .part no longer splits the panels

Changes in version 0.99.67 (2026-11-23)
+ New plotIntervals() draws time intervals of features, such as the
  significant intervals of MetaLonDA, from a table or metadata(x)

Changes in version 0.99.66 (2026-11-23)
+ plotTiles draws a results table per subject (group), such as
  miaTime::getShortTermChange() rates
+ Examples for miaTime stepwise divergence (plotTrend) and stability
  (plotFeatureScatter)

Changes in version 0.99.65 (2026-11-23)
+ plotTrend event labels in the right half end at their band, so they
  stay inside the plot
+ plotDirection draws with coord_radial() and writes direction labels
  along the circle, so faceted panels no longer overlap; requires
  ggplot2 4.0.0

Changes in version 0.99.64 (2026-11-23)
+ An interval between two samples takes group.by and facet.by from its
  later sample in every plot (plotDirection and plotTransitionMatrix
  used the earlier one)
+ plotComposition areas and streams break at gaps (max.gap), as lines do
+ plotLagHeatmap counts lags in visits for a visit factor
+ plotAlluvial orders numeric states as numbers

Changes in version 0.99.63 (2026-11-22)
+ The vignette is one analysis workflow covering all plot functions; the
  README has an example and a function-by-question table

Changes in version 0.99.62 (2026-11-22)
+ Shared helpers for visit gaps, grey and highlight levels, assay and
  presence checks, events legends and scalar checks; the package is
  about 90 lines shorter
+ POSIXct times in all plots (hours); plotSpectrum gives frequencies per
  hour for POSIXct; plotTiles takes detection
+ The single-sample warning gives the number of subjects

Changes in version 0.99.61 (2026-11-22)
+ Composition plots use the shared theme and palettes; "Other" is grey;
  top features through one helper; rank lines, transitions and turnover
  skip gaps (max.gap); presence through detection

Changes in version 0.99.60 (2026-11-22)
+ Trend and design plots use the shared theme and palettes; plotTrend
  lines break at skipped visits by default; plotSurvival takes detection

Changes in version 0.99.59 (2026-11-22)
+ Dynamics plots use the shared theme and palettes; correlation heatmaps
  are blue below 0 and red above; paths and moves skip gaps

Changes in version 0.99.58 (2026-11-22)
+ Every plot of one experiment takes a MultiAssayExperiment and
  experiment; plotLagHeatmap reads target from target.experiment
+ POSIXct times (distances and max.gap in hours)

Changes in version 0.99.57 (2026-11-22)
+ Added plotTimeEffect for effects over time (estimate and interval)
+ plotTrend: removed layout = "ridge", reference and limits; box and
  violin layouts separate group.by groups; clear errors for fit with
  rolling, period with events or fit tables, and align.to with NA
+ plotDOC: robust LOWESS curve as in Bashan et al. (2016)
+ plotSurvival: confidence band; dropout defined in the details
+ Subjects with NA are rejected; fixes in plotSwimmer, plotCalendar and
  plotDOC

Changes in version 0.99.56 (2026-11-22)
+ plotTBI: method = "sorensen" by default; bray needs absolute abundances
+ plotLagHeatmap: target read from assay.type; correlations within subjects
+ plotNetwork: directed edges with arrows, self-loops, undirected diff
+ plotSpectrum: Lomb-Scargle only (method removed)
+ plotTBI and plotFingerprint: time.point; ncomponents as in scater;
  facet.by for panels in plotDirection and plotIndividuality
+ Fixes in plotLagProfile, plotFingerprint, plotPath, plotFeatureScatter,
  plotTimeLoadings and plotDirection

Changes in version 0.99.55 (2026-11-22)
+ Removed plotAccumulation, plotReport, plotComposition(rank, y) and
  plotRanks(rank): agglomerate with mia::agglomerateByRank() first
+ plotComposition sums an existing "Other" feature into "Other"
+ plotTiles keeps Date times and breaks tiles at gaps (max.gap)
+ plotTransitionMatrix: as.relative and facet.by replace normalize and
  group.by
+ Fixes in plotHorizon, plotRanks, plotLandscape and plotTurnover

